1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,530
In Eritrea, a tourist needs a government
permit just to leave the capital.

2
00:00:04,770 --> 00:00:06,615
Not to enter a military base.

3
00:00:06,855 --> 00:00:08,164
Just to take a drive.

4
00:00:08,404 --> 00:00:11,611
And yet this locked-up country hides a
little Rome,

5
00:00:11,631 --> 00:00:14,458
a steam train, and a Tour de France
champion.

6
00:00:14,698 --> 00:00:18,461
Here is how a country can be this closed,
and this surprising.

7
00:00:18,701 --> 00:00:21,248
Stay for the coffee ceremony. It is the
best part.

8
00:00:21,487 --> 00:00:25,067
Eritrea sits on the Red Sea, in the Horn
of Africa.

9
00:00:25,307 --> 00:00:27,803
Its name comes from the Latin word for
that sea.

10
00:00:28,043 --> 00:00:31,497
About 6 million people live here, and the
capital is Asmara.

11
00:00:31,736 --> 00:00:34,668
Italy made Eritrea a colony in 1890.

12
00:00:34,909 --> 00:00:37,977
Then came British rule, then union with
Ethiopia.

13
00:00:38,217 --> 00:00:41,087
Eritreans fought for independence for
about 30 years.

14
00:00:41,328 --> 00:00:45,130
In 1993, 99.8 percent voted yes.

15
00:00:45,369 --> 00:00:47,644
The same president has led the country
ever

16
00:00:47,664 --> 00:00:50,365
since, and no national election has ever
been held.

17
00:00:50,605 --> 00:00:53,721
National service was meant to last 18
months.

18
00:00:53,961 --> 00:00:56,330
Human Rights Watch says many Eritreans
have

19
00:00:56,350 --> 00:00:58,442
spent their whole working lives in it.

20
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:01,001
That is the backdrop for the rules
visitors face.

21
00:01:01,241 --> 00:01:03,685
So what can you see inside the capital?

22
00:01:03,926 --> 00:01:06,987
Asmara is full of Italian buildings from
the 1930s.

23
00:01:07,226 --> 00:01:12,419
UNESCO listed the city in 2017, the first
modernist World Heritage site in Africa.

24
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,816
The star is a gas station.

25
00:01:14,936 --> 00:01:18,710
The Fiat Tagliero, finished in 1938, looks
like an airplane.

26
00:01:18,949 --> 00:01:22,739
Its wings were hit during World War Two,
and they did not collapse.

27
00:01:22,979 --> 00:01:24,321
Then there is the train.

28
00:01:24,561 --> 00:01:27,538
A steam train still climbs from the Red
Sea port

29
00:01:27,558 --> 00:01:30,971
of Massawa up to Asmara, more than 2
kilometers higher.

30
00:01:31,211 --> 00:01:34,298
Italians started building that line in
1887.

31
00:01:34,538 --> 00:01:37,450
It reopened in 2003 after years of ruin.

32
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:39,974
At the bottom, Massawa has coral stone

33
00:01:39,994 --> 00:01:42,581
buildings, and boats to the Dahlak
islands.

34
00:01:42,821 --> 00:01:46,198
There are more than 200 of them, and you
need a permit to go.

35
00:01:46,439 --> 00:01:47,554
Now, the culture.

36
00:01:47,793 --> 00:01:50,273
Eritrean life runs on coffee.

37
00:01:50,513 --> 00:01:52,040
The ceremony is called bun.

38
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:55,156
The host roasts green beans in front of
you, grinds

39
00:01:55,176 --> 00:01:59,178
them, and brews them in a clay pot called
a jebena. Incense burns.

40
00:01:59,418 --> 00:02:02,308
Then come three cups, each weaker than the
last.

41
00:02:02,548 --> 00:02:05,399
It is a sign of respect, and it is never
rushed.

42
00:02:05,638 --> 00:02:06,941
Meals are shared too.

43
00:02:07,182 --> 00:02:09,611
Stews called tsebhi are scooped up with

44
00:02:09,631 --> 00:02:12,374
injera, a sour flatbread, from one big
tray.

45
00:02:12,614 --> 00:02:15,090
Italian dishes are part of Eritrean
cooking as well.

46
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:17,523
Now, what does $10 get you?

47
00:02:17,764 --> 00:02:20,912
The official rate is 15 nakfa to one
dollar.

48
00:02:21,151 --> 00:02:23,519
So $10 is 150 nakfa.

49
00:02:23,759 --> 00:02:26,459
A plate at a local eatery runs about $2 to
$5.

50
00:02:26,699 --> 00:02:28,653
A local beer is around $1 or $2.

51
00:02:28,893 --> 00:02:30,545
A cappuccino, about $1.

52
00:02:30,786 --> 00:02:33,793
Sources disagree on prices, so treat these
as estimates.

53
00:02:34,033 --> 00:02:36,703
The catch is that Eritrea runs on cash.

54
00:02:36,943 --> 00:02:39,226
Foreign cards do not work at ATMs.

55
00:02:39,466 --> 00:02:40,616
Now for the best part.

56
00:02:40,856 --> 00:02:43,205
Cycling is a national passion here.

57
00:02:43,445 --> 00:02:48,344
The Italians brought it, and by the 1930s
and 1940s, clubs were forming in Asmara.

58
00:02:48,584 --> 00:02:52,169
Today, thousands line the streets on
Sundays to cheer the races.

59
00:02:52,408 --> 00:02:55,103
In 2024, Biniam Girmay, a rider born in

60
00:02:55,123 --> 00:02:58,376
Asmara, won three stages at the Tour de
France.

61
00:02:58,616 --> 00:03:01,613
He became the first Black African to win a
stage of the Tour.

62
00:03:01,854 --> 00:03:04,930
And he took the green jersey, a first for
an African rider.

63
00:03:05,170 --> 00:03:07,138
When he came home, thousands of people

64
00:03:07,158 --> 00:03:09,388
lined the streets of Asmara to welcome
him.

65
00:03:09,628 --> 00:03:10,895
One more thing before you pack.

66
00:03:11,134 --> 00:03:12,214
The don't list.

67
00:03:12,454 --> 00:03:14,816
Don't leave Asmara without a travel
permit.

68
00:03:15,056 --> 00:03:18,034
Foreigners need one even to go beyond the
capital's province.

69
00:03:18,274 --> 00:03:20,732
Don't photograph military or government
buildings.

70
00:03:20,972 --> 00:03:24,426
Visitors have faced warnings, confiscated
phones, and arrest.

71
00:03:24,665 --> 00:03:26,195
Don't change money on the street.

72
00:03:26,436 --> 00:03:29,057
Government rules say to use official
exchange offices.

73
00:03:29,297 --> 00:03:31,308
Don't go near the Ethiopian border.

74
00:03:31,547 --> 00:03:34,023
Landmines remain, and tensions are high.

75
00:03:34,263 --> 00:03:36,603
And don't visit the tank graveyard without
a permit.

76
00:03:36,843 --> 00:03:39,609
It needs one, even inside the capital.
That is Eritrea.

77
00:03:39,850 --> 00:03:43,233
Closed roads, open coffee, and a capital
that looks like a dream.

78
00:03:43,472 --> 00:03:45,942
Which country should we visit next? Tell
me in the comments.

